# {{ title }}

A module for [Atrium](https://github.com/AlveBy/atrium).

## Install

```bash
composer require {{ package }}
php artisan atrium:module:install {{ package }}
```

Add `--demo` to fill it with three example records. `php artisan atrium:module:remove {{ package }}` takes it out and asks whether to keep its data.

## What is inside

- `composer.json`: the manifest in `extra.atrium` (models, migrations, demo seeder). Add `settings`, `permissions`, `public_urls`, `search` or `submodules` there as the module grows: see the [module docs](https://github.com/AlveBy/atrium/blob/main/docs/modules.md).
- `src/Models/{{ model }}.php`: the model, with its admin form and list. It uses the record cache (`Cacheable`, `CachesRecords`): read lists with `cachedPaginate()` or `cachedCards()`, see the [cache docs](https://github.com/AlveBy/atrium/blob/main/docs/cache.md).
- `database/migrations`: its table.
- `src/Database/{{ class }}DemoSeeder.php`: the demo content.
- `tests`: Orchestra Testbench tests that install the module in a bare Atrium.
- `.github/workflows/tests.yml`: the tests on PHP 8.3 and 8.4.

## Tests

```bash
composer install
vendor/bin/phpunit
```

## Publishing

The `"type": "atrium-module"` and the `atrium-module` keyword put the package in the catalogue on every Atrium site's Modules screen once it is on [Packagist](https://packagist.org/packages/submit).
